the recent covent surge taking a toll on  many local businesses including the  regional transportation commission which  is struggling with a shortage of bus  drivers mary jane belliesa joins us live  with what you need to know if you take  the bus to get around town  yeah you know bus leaders are  apologizing to passengers in advance for  these delays and you know unfortunately  rotc says that these shortages aren't  specific to certain bus routes as they  struggle to figure out what bus drivers  are available for what day  rtc deputy ceo francis julian says a  rise in omicron coveted cases is  responsible for its labor shortage  julian says rtc is working on short-term  mitigation strategies and service  changes to address these issues in the  meantime julian asks passengers to be  patient respectful and courteous to  drivers as they're pulling extra shifts  we have in between 50 and 80 operators  that are out either because because  they're quarantined out of caution or  because they contracted  covid so it is challenging our service  is  once again it's a fluid situation where  we're seeing disruption in between three  and six percent on a day-to-day basis  the rtc has posted open positions on its  website for drivers and mechanics  now this transit app can help you track  the bus routes bus wait times and what  delays to expect reporting live here at  the bonneville transit center mary jane  vallieza live local now
 

